    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Viktor says he needs to work. Lanovsky starts monologuing about how people call him a scary person because he hunts people without documents. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, давайте только быстро.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я перейду сразу к делу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вы слышали что-нибудь обо мне?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, слышали во всех странах.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Знаете, как меня называют?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Меня называют страшным человеком.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Месяц назад была проверка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Они ничего тут не нашли.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мятную конфету не желаете?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, мне не нужно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Наша служба похожа на птиц.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мы всегда смотрим на вас сверху.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, давайте только быстро.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, let us just do it quickly.' Chef Viktor starts with 'good' and pairs it with 'let's' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я перейду сразу к делу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will get straight to the point.' the speaker puts 'I' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'to cross'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вы слышали что-нибудь обо мне?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Have you heard anything about me?' Here 'you' sets up the idea, while 'to me' comes at the end for emphasis. Chef Viktor answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, слышали во всех странах.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, heard in all countries.' You'll hear 'did you hear?' all the time in the show, here connected with 'country'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Знаете, как меня называют?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you know what they call me?' The key word here means 'know', which the speaker combines with 'how'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Меня называют страшным человеком.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They call me a scary person.' Notice the word order: 'me' comes first, and 'person' finishes the sentence. Then Chef Viktor replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Месяц назад была проверка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'A month ago there was an inspection.' The key word here means 'month', which Chef Viktor combines with 'ago'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Они ничего тут не нашли.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They did not find anything here.' The first content word means 'they', and 'found' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мятную конфету не желаете?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you want a mint candy?' A compact expression built around 'mint' and 'would you like'. And Chef Viktor jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, мне не нужно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, I do not need it.' Here 'to me' sets up the idea, while 'necessary' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Наша служба похожа на птиц.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Our service is like birds.' Listen for the word meaning 'service' right alongside 'similar' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мы всегда смотрим на вас сверху.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We always look at you from above.' the speaker uses the polite plural 'you' here alongside 'we', keeping a formal or respectful tone. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
